00:00:45.095 --> 00:00:46.720
But it's around the
Internet of Things,

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.670
connecting things
to the internet.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.880
And within IoT, there is a
couple of different angles.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.940
One is technical.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.060
We hear a lot about
IoT technologies--

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.510
MQTT, and TLS, and lots
of three-letter acronyms.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.489
And that is important.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:05.030
But there's a whole
other side of it,

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.490
which is IoT's not
just a technology,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.820
but it's a whole new
business venture.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.680
I don't know about
the folks in the room,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.880
but I haven't met my
first chief IoT officer.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.920
So IoT is still very new.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.960
And many enterprises
are trying to figure out

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.510
how it fits into their
organization as part of that.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:27.070
And one key aspect of it is ROI.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.020
Where is the money
in this stuff?

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.830
And a lot of the companies that
we work with and that we see

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.330
are trying to figure that out.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.220
So, quick introductions,
and we'll dive right in.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:38.980
So I'm Adam Michelson.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:43.300
And I'm a product manager
inside of Google IoT Core,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.240
which is Google's IoT offering.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.600
So my job is to build
some of that tech

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.910
to make sure IoT
products are safe,

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.160
