00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.676
So, let me take you through a
little bit of the experience

00:18:36.676 --> 00:18:37.689
of Deep Sky Vineyard.

00:18:37.689 --> 00:18:38.980
This is about two minutes long.

00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:40.420
[VIDEO PLAYBACK]

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:42.800
[SOFT, MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:47.020
- Farming, it's the
oldest industry on earth

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.370
and arguably the most important.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:53.680
It feeds the world, employs
millions, sustains life.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:55.720
And it's under siege.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:58.870
Agriculture consumes 70% of
the world's water, its most

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:00.430
precious resource.

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.410
A single almond the
size of a thumbprint

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.770
requires just over a
gallon to reach maturity.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.810
Put another way, that
water that California

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:10.780
uses in a single year
just to grow almonds

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:13.390
is enough to serve all
the homes and businesses

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:17.770
in the Greater Los Angeles
area for nearly three years.

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:21.070
Farmers rely on diverse data
and generations of accumulated

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:23.320
experience to do what they do.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:24.760
But farming is still farming.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.010
And operating margins are slim.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:28.870
The oldest industry
on earth also

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:33.210
has the oldest challenge--
consume less, produce.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.860
The data that empowers
21st century farming

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.660
pours in from
sensors in the ground

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.390
that measure moisture
content from water volume

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:43.600
monitors deep in the aquifer,
from weather stations,

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.690
and from generations of
experience and knowledge.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.140
But here's the challenge.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:51.370
How can all that data become
a single, meaningful real-time

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:54.340
indicator of how
the crop is doing?

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:57.010
Well, there is a solution.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.410
Imagine that you're a vineyard
operator with the ability

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:02.710
to log into a mobile app
to see contextualized data

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:05.140
from thousands of sensors
telling you everything that's

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.140
happening in your
vineyard, in real time,

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.050
from anywhere in the world.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:11.390
That same app helps you
anticipate and respond

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:14.840
to equipment before they
occur through rich, predictive

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:17.000
insight and provides
detailed information

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.950
about the vineyard's
micro climate.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:24.520
Imagine receiving requests for
water directly from the plants

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.290
and having a system that
can automatically respond,

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.080
or being able to
focus specifically

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.650
on one row of vines or on
the data from a single plant.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.690
Imagine being able
to view and analyze

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.820
the color of the
grapes on that plant

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:39.340
or the ratio of the
sun above the canopy

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:42.782
to the shade below it.

00:20:42.782 --> 00:20:45.370
This Is precision agriculture.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.770
This is nio.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:50.130
We combine millions of
unrelated, complex data points

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:53.070
and convert them into a simple,
visual, richly insightful

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:54.300
experience.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:57.840
And the result, lower cost in
resource consumption, higher

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:01.110
crop yields, and
better product quality.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:04.290
Precision agriculture is a
game changer for farming.

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:07.170
When experience combines
with real time data collected

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:10.530
at the plants themselves, we
redefine the world's oldest

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:12.450
and most revered industry.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:17.075
And that is only the beginning.

00:21:17.075 --> 00:21:18.001
